{"key":"umbra","name":"Umbra","accent":"#ff3a22","based":"Mesa/Boogie Mark V","intro":"Umbra is now a full Mark V: three channels, each with three modes, just like the real amp. CHANNEL picks 1, 2 or 3 and MODE picks that channel's voicing. Each channel remembers its own mode and knob settings.","notes":["Channel 1 and 2: where the pack has low, mid and high gain captures (Tweed, Edge, Crunch, Mark I), Gain blends between them.","Channel 3 was captured at high gain with three EQ voicings: scoop, balanced and mids. Middle crossfades between those three real captures, then the tone stack shapes the rest.","Extras not on the panel: Black Metal I/II and boosted versions (808, TS9, SD-1) of the high-gain modes. These could be used automatically when one of those pedals is switched on in front.","Most accurate pack after the IIC+ (median accuracy score 0.0105, lower is better)."],"W":1768,"H":709,"skins":[{"id":"umbra_mk5","ptrOff":true}],"knobs":[{"label":"Gain","b":[305,532,119,119],"o":[49.63,49.874],"c":[364.1,591.4],"r":48.2,"v":0.62},{"label":"Treble","b":[445,532,119,119],"o":[50.345,49.874],"c":[504.9,591.4],"r":48.2,"v":0.45},{"label":"Middle","b":[564,532,119,119],"o":[50.025,49.874],"c":[623.5,591.4],"r":48.2,"v":0.55},{"label":"Bass","b":[683,532,119,119],"o":[49.697,49.874],"c":[742.1,591.4],"r":48.2,"v":0.6},{"label":"Presence","b":[801,532,119,119],"o":[50.218,49.874],"c":[860.8,591.4],"r":48.2,"v":0.4},{"label":"Master","b":[963,523,137,137],"o":[49.832,49.891],"c":[1031.3,591.4],"r":55.9,"v":0.5},{"label":"Output","b":[1120,532,119,119],"o":[50.034,49.874],"c":[1179.5,591.4],"r":48.2,"v":0.35}],"leds":{"ch1":[1297,550,22,20],"ch2":[1312,550,22,20],"ch3":[1327,550,22,20],"md1":[1400,550,22,20],"md2":[1415,550,22,20],"md3":[1429,550,22,20]},"buttons":{"channel":[1305.4,581.8,38.3,25.0],"mode":[1408.4,581.8,38.3,25.0]},"power":[192.4,588.7,26.4],"dims":[{"id":"channel","names":["Channel 1","Channel 2","Channel 3"],"button":"channel","leds":[["ch1"],["ch2"],[